EDIT(1)

NAME
     edit - a simple screen editor

SYNOPSIS
     edit [-ilv] [-T tabsize] [+line[,column]] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
     edit is a screen editor in the style of nano. The top line shows the
     file name and whether it has been modified; the bottom lines show a
     status message and the main commands. Type to insert text; the
     keys below do everything else (^ is Ctrl; M- is Esc or Alt).

     Files and exit
       ^O        write the file (asks for the name)
       ^X        exit, asking to save changes; with several files, go to
                 the next one
       ^R        insert another file at the cursor
       ^G        show the key bindings

     Moving
       arrows    ^B ^F ^P ^N        ^A Home / ^E End (Home toggles
                                    between the indentation and column 1)
       ^Y PgUp   ^V PgDn            ^Left ^Right   by words
       M-\ ^Home first line         M-/ ^End       last line
       ^_ M-G    go to line[,column]   M-]  matching bracket
       ^C        show the cursor position

     Editing
       Backspace ^H, Del ^D   delete       Enter   new line (auto-indent
                                           with -i or M-I)
       ^K   cut the line (repeat to cut several) or the marked text
       ^U   paste                          M-6  copy
       ^^ M-A  set or clear the mark (select text with the cursor)
       ^J   justify the paragraph (fill to 72 columns)
       M-U  undo                           M-E  redo

     Searching
       ^W   search forward      ^Q   search backward
       M-W  repeat the search   ^\   search and replace (Y/N/A)
       A search is case-insensitive unless it contains capitals.

     Display
       M-N  line numbers (also -l)         ^L   redraw
       C, assembly, shell and Rust files are syntax highlighted.

OPTIONS
     -i  auto-indent       -l  line numbers      -v  view only
     -T  tab width (default 8)
     +N  start at line N (and column after a comma)

SEE ALSO
     more(1)
